verdict:
The load-carrying bottom of P_sachta will not break off. The hub disc (1.25) and back floor are bonded over 442 mm2 to the brass 36T gear. Pressing the head down hard (2 x L2) puts 0.2 MPa on the hub disc, which is backed by brass (margin 64). Lifting the robot by the head (2 x L1) peels the bond at 0.20 MPa including the x3 peel factor (margin 13), and the DIN 9021 washer cannot pass the gear bore even with a 0.5 chamfer. The slim corners measure 1.21 / 1.34 and print fine.

The real-life weak points at the bottom are not the resin walls:
(1) MAJOR: F15 (M3x6) has only 0.8 mm of thread in the aluminium bridge and strips at 0.18-0.46 N.m, which a normal screwdriver or L-key reaches. Fix: M3x8 + 2 x DIN 125 on the DIN 9021, giving 0.49-1.04 N.m; every clearance stays >= 1.0 (head 1.85 below the neck).
(2) MAJOR: the drum shroud's free arch (az ~76-126) is not joined to the floor and has sharp roots. It breaks at about 8-19 N sideways and prints as an unsupported 9.6 mm bridge. It carries no load, but it is the piece most likely to chip. Fix: a web r 15.1-15.5 plus a relief in the lift-module plate, or at least supports on the arch and careful handling.

Minor items, all without space cost:
- print text: allow supports on the hub-disc landing face, then sand it flat;
- drill the T_cap hole to D3.1 and abrade the aluminium;
- use a toughened epoxy;
- Loctite 222 on F10, and measure the insert before drilling;
- grease and inspect the PTFE tape;
- R0.5-1 at the window corners;
- avoid long holds at mid lift.

Status: buildable after the two fixes and the notes.

Files are in /tmp/claude-0/gapwf/fin/T4/sachta_b/: scripts m04_geom_check.py and m05_calcs.py with their .json outputs, and r02_label.py, which produced the three labelled 1200 px images r02_zdola.png, r02_rez_x0.png and r02_rez_roh.png (I looked at all three). report.md was NOT written, because the harness blocks report files for subagents; this structured result is the report.

Corrections to the paused run:
- the 0.047 / 0.353 corner minima were rays grazing the window jambs;
- an off-centre bond does not cause binding;
- a bore chamfer does not lose the retention;
- the F15 fix now includes the screw-length tolerance;
- the drop mass now includes the collar disc (46 g).
